          "event_id": "81c4b0d9-582d-4d7f-88db-a8bfbe95075a",
          "session_id": "bench_027bcfe5",
          "event_type": "agent_response",
          "payload": {
            "text": "That sounds like a fantastic workshop — making fresh pasta from scratch is so rewarding. I can help you turn this into a message, thank-you note, social post, or draft an email. Here are a few ready-to-use options — tell me which one to send or save as a draft and give me the recipient(s) or platform:\n\n1) Quick message to Lisa\n   Subject: Had a blast at Chef Mia's workshop!\n   Body:\n   \"Lisa — I had so much fun at Chef Mia's Culinary Studio this weekend. Making spaghetti alla carbonara and fettuccine Alfredo from scratch with you was such a great hands-on experience. I can’t wait to try the recipes at home — want to get together next weekend to test them?\"\n\n2) Thank-you email to Chef Mia\n   Subject: Thank you — Pasta Workshop\n   Body:\n   \"Chef Mia — Thank you for the wonderful weekend workshop. Learning to make traditional Italian pasta from scratch, especially the spaghetti alla carbonara and fettuccine Alfredo, was fantastic. I appreciated the hands-on approach and your helpful tips — I’m excited to practice these recipes at home. Do you share the recipes or a resource list from the class?\"\n\n3) Short social post\n   \"Just finished a weekend pasta workshop at Chef Mia's Culinary Studio with my friend Lisa — we learned to make spaghetti alla carbonara and fettuccine Alfredo from scratch. The hands-on experience was fantastic — can’t wait to try these recipes at home! #homemadepasta #foodie\"\n\n4) Announcement to friends/family (email)\n   Subject: I learned to make fresh pasta!\n   Body:\n   \"Hi everyone — I attended a pasta workshop at Chef Mia’s with Lisa and learned to make spaghetti alla carbonara and fettuccine Alfredo from scratch. It was a hands-on class and I’m excited to try the recipes at home. Who wants to come over for a pasta night soon?\"\n\n5) Personal recipe note / blog paragraph\n   \"This weekend I attended Chef Mia’s Culinary Studio with my friend Lisa and learned to make traditional Italian pasta from scratch. We practiced spaghetti alla carbonara and fettuccine Alfredo — the hands-on instruction made the techniques click. Can’t wait to recreate them at home and tweak the flavors.\"\n\nWhat would you like me to do next?\n- Send or draft one of these (tell me which number and give recipient email/address or say 'draft')\n- Edit any of the messages first (tell me what to change)\n- Create a tailored social post for a specific platform (Instagram, Facebook, Twitter/X — and whether to include photos)"
          }
